1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,840
JONATHAN LaPAGLIA:
Give me your torch.

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,640
The tribe has spoken.

3
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,920
(OVER RADIO) Flight 111,
you're clear for landing. Runway 3.

4
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,320
Roger.

5
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:52,240
Abort! Abort!
There's a person on the runway.

6
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,080
Of course I had to come out
of maternity leave for this.

7
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,160
What would a global showdown be
without me?

8
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:11,760
I have played the most days
of Australian Survivor

9
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:13,160
out of any person.

10
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:15,680
I have done my bit,

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,520
and I need to get paid.

12
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,440
I still don't have a Chanel bag,

13
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:22,520
and as always, I wouldn't mind
a little tan top-up.

14
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:31,520
JONATHAN: This season,

15
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:36,800
seven of Australia's best
are taking to the beaches of Samoa.

16
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,800
Surprise, mother trucker!

17
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,000
(LAUGHS)

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,280
The king of the jungle
is back, baby.

19
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,480
# Da-da-da! #

20
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,680
It's like I'm in the Olympics

21
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,640
for lying, cheating
and stealing.

22
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,920
(LAUGHS)

23
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:01,160
This is my third season,

24
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,720
and there is
a long list of things

25
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:07,160
that you haven't even
seen me do yet,

26
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,160
which is, like...
one of them would be win.

27
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,720
(LAUGHS)

28
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:18,640
Fighting for the title
is a devious mastermind...

29
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:25,200
..and a strategic rebel.

30
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,920
I am now a part of history,

31
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:32,480
playing against
the world's best.

32
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,840
But I'm the rebel queen.

33
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,360
The last time I played,

34
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,000
every move that I made
was a blindside.

35
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,480
So, this season,
I've got that taste in my mouth

36
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,040
and I want it back.

37
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:50,720
Joining them is
the godmother of negotiation.

38
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,960
People see me as
a hard-nosed bitch
businessperson

39
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:59,640
because I can wheel and deal
like the best of them.

40
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,720
And a mad king.

41
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:09,240
I've grown a lot as a person

42
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,520
since the last time
I played Survivor.

43
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:16,200
My arse has doubled in size.

44
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,240
I'm coming in hot
with this dad bod.

45
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:23,560
The motto I live by
is "glory or death".

46
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:27,080
Nobody has been a more powerful
player in Australian Survivor

47
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,600
than me.

48
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,080
Nobody.

49
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:42,880
I played basically
the perfect game of Survivor

50
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:46,240
and I won
half a million dollars.

51
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,160
That was the completion
of a dream.

52
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:53,440
If there was one thing

53
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:56,160
that was going to make me
play this game again,

54
00:03:56,160 --> 00:04:01,840
it's to represent my country
and play on behalf of Australia.

55
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,440
We're not looking for
the goat "maaa-aa-aa".

56
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,800
We're looking for the GOAT -

57
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:19,320
the greatest of all time.

58
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:26,640
Golden God is back!

59
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,080
Uhhh!

60
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:32,840
This is a tribe
of extraordinary players.

61
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,360
(HORN HONKS)

62
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,120
SHONEE: Ahh! (LAUGHS)
Who is that?

63
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,760
Giants of the game.

64
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:40,200
Yo!
(ALL EXCLAIM AND CHEER)

65
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,840
(LAUGHS)

66
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:47,040
With a history rich in rivalry
and old bonds.

67
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,840
(BOTH LAUGH)

68
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,800
I thought, there's no way.

69
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,600
(BOTH LAUGH)

70
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:58,720
But now they have to face
their toughest opponents yet.

71
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,200
The World.

72
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,200
At the helm
of the invading force...

73
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,120
..the USA,

74
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:13,360
where it all began.

75
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,800
I would say
I'm a Survivor legend.

76
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:20,000
I played Survivor three times
and I won twice.

77
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,160
I won ¤3 million.

78
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:26,560
Right now, this season of
Survivor is going to be short
and fast,

79
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,760
and that's my gameplay.

80
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,080
I'm fast and I'm furious.

81
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,840
I hit the ground running,

82
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:32,360
and when it's on, it's on.

83
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,440
King of the jungle.

84
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,960
I'm building a spy shack.

85
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,080
Spy nest. And I'm
going to hear everything.

86
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,800
The winner of Survivor Cagayan,
Tony.

87
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,720
But this time around,
I'm not here for the money.

88
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,160
I'm here for the glory.

89
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:48,600
I want the world title
of Sole Survivor.

90
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,960
These are the originals.

91
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,960
Legends who broke the mould...

92
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:03,560
..and built a reputation
of cutthroat gameplay.

93
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,960
Oh, sweet little baby Aussies.

94
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:11,880
Think they know how to play
Survivor. They're so cute.

95
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,280
(LAUGHS)

96
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:18,640
I've been playing this game
for decades. For decades.

97
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:21,760
This will be my fifth time
playing Survivor.

98
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:24,280
Everyone all said that I'm
the most dangerous player
out here,

99
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,880
so...I guess they're right.

100
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,080
The winner of Survivor
Fans Vs Favourites.

101
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:31,240
So, I've won it once,
I should have won it twice,

102
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:34,440
and I'm here to win it again
on the world stage.

103
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,240
The last time
I was here in Samoa,

104
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,480
I had a bitter jury,

105
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,360
so I lost by a few votes.

106
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:46,440
So I am here to claim the win
that was meant to be mine

107
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,640
16 years ago.

108
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:56,440
They'll be joined by the best
the world has to offer.

109
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,080
A deadly triple threat.

110
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:09,640
I was in season 2
of Survivor Quebec, and...

111
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:10,800
(SPEAKS QUEBEC FRENCH)

112
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,480
A strategic assassin.

113
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:19,040
I'm the once and forever
reigning champion

114
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,560
of Survivor New Zealand.

115
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:23,400
(LAUGHS) Because it got
cancelled after I won.

116
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,120
And the Nordic wolf.

117
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,560
No-one knows this guy
from Finland.

118
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,080
You're gonna be surprised.

119
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,120
He got game.

120
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:40,800
I smile a lot, but, like,
this is my poker face.

121
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:47,880
And completing this tribe,
a charming puppet-master.

122
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:53,480
I played Survivor South Africa
once before, and I won.

123
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,680
My eyes. They have
the ability to hypnotise.

124
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:02,560
Gets very dangerous
the longer you're around me.

125
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,640
My sole objective

126
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:07,320
is to restore balance
to the world of Survivor.

127
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,160
You've got Australians
running around

128
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,720
calling themselves
gods and kings.

129
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:17,280
So I'm here to give them
a long-overdue
devil of a thrashing,

130
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:19,280
compliments of Africa.

131
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,120
(LAUGHS)

132
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:26,480
The Aussies must unite
and see past their differences

133
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:30,240
to defeat
these international
heavyweights.

134
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:34,240
It's a battle
25 years in the making.

135
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:38,440
Best of the best going head
to head for that ultimate title.

136
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,920
This is Australia
versus the World.

137
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:48,320
16 days, 14 people,
one survivor.

138
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,960
Come on in.

139
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,880
LUKE: Oooh.

140
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,240
Hello, hello.
Yeah. (CHUCKLES)

141
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,680
Well, hello.

142
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,240
Jonathan.

143
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:30,560
GEORGE: Long time, no see, JLP.
Long time, no see.

144
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,120
Welcome back.

145
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,000
Wow.

146
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
There you have it.

147
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:39,000
The seven of you represent

148
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,160
some of the best players
Australia has to offer.

149
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,760
And I think it's fair to say

150
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:46,560
your gameplay is up there
with the best in the world.

151
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,720
Indeed.

152
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:51,880
So I sent out a few invitations
to see what would happen

153
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:54,840
when the best of Australian
Survivor

154
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,440
goes up against
the best in the world.

155
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,880
Wow.

156
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,040
Come on in.

157
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:02,560
LUKE: Hey! Who we got here?
SARAH: Oh, my God. Here we go.

158
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,800
Oh, my...

159
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,520
Oh, my God, it's Cirie.

160
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,800
I heard my name. Great.

161
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:14,600
GEORGE: Oh, my God, those guns!

162
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,480
Rob Bentele
might be the biggest unit here.

163
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,560
Wow.
Bloody hell.

164
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,600
What, what, what!

165
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,800
Parv on the end.

166
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,440
Hi, Parv!
Hi!

167
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,000
Well, this is quite the line-up.

168
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:36,360
First of all, I want to thank
you for accepting our invitation

169
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,920
and coming out to play
Australian Survivor.

170
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,640
We really appreciate that.

171
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:43,720
The seven of you are some
of the greatest, most iconic

172
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:47,120
and devastatingly effective
players the world has ever seen,

173
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,240
and you've travelled a long way
to get here -

174
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,800
from the US, South Africa,

175
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,000
New Zealand, Quebec

176
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,520
and as far as Finland.

177
00:10:55,520 --> 00:11:00,400
And personally, I'd like to
thank you for coming out here

178
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,680
to show these Aussies
just how it's done.

179
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,360
Thank you for inviting us.

180
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,560
Welcome to
Australia Versus The World.

181
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,720
(ALL CHEER)

182
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,800
This is so good.

183
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,920
So, Shonee.
Yes.

184
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:19,360
You've played a lot of Survivor.

185
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:21,440
Maybe not quite as much as
Parvati.

186
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,640
I mean, she has, you know,
more days than you in the game.

187
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:27,360
But you're right up there,
no doubt.
Thanks.

188
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,840
So what keeps bringing you back?

189
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:31,960
It's just like this love/hate
relationship with this game.

190
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:34,640
You think you're retired and
you're like, "Yep, I'm done,"

191
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,400
and then next minute
you're like, "Fine,

192
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,480
"I'll buy a little red tee dress
and I'll be back."

193
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:41,640
Can't keep me away.

194
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,800
So, Kirby,

195
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,920
there's four winners over there
and only one over here.

196
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:49,240
Actually, Tony's a two-time
winner, so technically,
it's five winners.

197
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,880
Thanks for that, Jonathan.
You bet.

198
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:54,280
I mean, isn't that just
a little bit intimidating?

199
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:59,040
Well, I'm the baby of the group -
I've only played once,

200
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,160
and I didn't watch it
before coming on,

201
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:05,240
so...I've kept that the same,
so I don't know any of youse,

202
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:08,600
which...I don't know, that
could be a detriment, maybe.

203
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,280
It could work in my advantage.

204
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,320
Well, Tony,
I'm kind of surprised.

205
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:18,040
I expected some trash talk
from the Aussies,
but there's nothing.

206
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:20,320
No, they're a lovely
bunch of people.

207
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:23,640
Um... However, I do think
that they did make a mistake.

208
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,920
The world title is at stake.

209
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,040
This ain't just
a regular Sole Survivor title.

210
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,200
This is the world title.

211
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,000
I think we're ready to lose
limbs out here for that.

212
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,560
So, Cirie, you're known as

213
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:40,560
the greatest Survivor player
that has never won.

214
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,960
Wah-wah.
Wah-wah. I know.

215
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,360
(OTHERS LAUGH)

216
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:46,600
Is this game
going to change that?

217
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,720
Well, that remains to be seen,
doesn't it, Jonathan?

218
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,960
I'm here, and I'm here
like Tony -
I'm here to lose a limb.

219
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:58,520
Alright, well, it's clear you've
all come out to play,
and play hard.

220
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:02,600
But make no mistake, this is
going to be a season
like no other.

221
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:05,800
It is going to be fast.
It is going to be furious.

222
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,720
And not only are you
from different countries,

223
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,800
but you're from different worlds
of Survivor.

224
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,960
But in the end,
it's going to come down to

225
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,480
those three little
magical words -

226
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,840
outwit, outplay, and outlast -

227
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:19,120
and whoever does it the best

228
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:21,200
is going to walk out of here
with a quarter million dollars,

229
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,720
but maybe more importantly,

230
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:27,000
with the title of the greatest
Survivor player of all time.

231
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,320
Wow.

232
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,520
Is it going to be an Aussie?

233
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,880
Is it going to be someone
from the World tribe?

234
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:37,560
We'll find out
in 16 very intense days.

235
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:39,280
Alright, enough of me talking.

236
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,240
You're gonna need these.

237
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,080
(SQUEALS)
Well done, Shon.

238
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:50,560
Well done, Shonee!
That IS a great start.

239
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,720
Go ahead. Put them on.

240
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,520
Oh, gimme that buff!

241
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:56,400
No, I...I missed the invite.

242
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,400
Cute!
CIRIE: And go, baby!

243
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:07,480
Alright. Are you ready to get
to your first reward challenge?

244
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,960
Yes!
Yes, sir!

245
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,920
For today's challenge...

246
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,720
..you're going to
race down a slide...

247
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,400
..scramble under a net,

248
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,920
and then throw sandbags
at a bell.

249
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,040
First person to ring the bell...

250
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,360
(DING!)

251
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,960
..will get to choose one item
from this shelf.

252
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,200
Want to know
what you're playing for?

253
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,240
Yeah.
Sure.

254
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,520
Everything you need...

255
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:41,360
Look at that!
Oh, my goodness gracious.

256
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,320
..to kick-start your game.

257
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,880
Tarp. Comfort items.

258
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:48,880
Basket of fruit. Tea and coffee.

259
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:52,640
Shonee, some champagne
to celebrate that first day.

260
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,240
Yeah, it's a celebration!

261
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:57,160
The all-important flint.

262
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,280
Boring.

263
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,320
(OTHERS LAUGH)

264
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,120
And whatever's in this box.

265
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:06,280
Oooh!
Ohh.

266
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,320
Oh. I think we need that.

267
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:11,960
Worth playing for?
ALL: Yes!

268
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:14,320
Alright, I'm going to give you
a minute to strategise,

269
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,920
and then we're gonna get it on.
Let's go!

270
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,080
Booyah!

271
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,360
What's in the box?!

272
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,120
Jeepers creepers.

273
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:43,840
Alright, Aussies,
who do you want to put up?

274
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,080
The Golden God.

275
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:46,680
For green and gold.

276
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,920
Come on, golden boy.

277
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,160
Might as well.
Are you gonna go?

278
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,440
Alright, come on, Rob, let's go.

279
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,400
(OTHERS SHOUT SUPPORT)

280
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,640
GEORGE: Go get him.
Let's go!

281
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:01,320
South Africa!

282
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,120
DAVID: Hey, I got
a proposition for you.

283
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,800
Yeah?
I want you in the end game.

284
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:09,320
I think, like, uh, I go, you go.

285
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,760
So I need you deep, dude.

286
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,520
They're going to be
coming for us super early.

287
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,720
So here's my proposition.

288
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,560
Yeah?
I will give you input

289
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,640
into who goes home
on the Australian tribe

290
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:23,440
if you do the same thing for me.

291
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:26,800
You played one of the greatest
games I've ever seen, brother.
OK?

292
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:32,320
Think on it. You can tell me
after. Give me the signal.

293
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:35,000
Alright, here we go.
First round.

294
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
We have the Golden God
from Australia

295
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,760
taking on Zulu Rob
from the World.

296
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,800
That's a lot of beef up there.

297
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,000
(LAUGHS) Grade A.

298
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,360
For reward, Survivors ready?

299
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,120
Go!

300
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:55,320
(ONLOOKERS CHEER
AND SHOUT SUPPORT)

301
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:56,800
Rob gets the jump.

302
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,640
GEORGE: Wow, what a transition!

303
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,240
SHONEE: It was like a fish!

304
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:03,360
David trying to catch him.

305
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,680
They both get to the sandbags.
(DING!)

306
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:08,000
Rob takes it out. Hits the bell.

307
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,920
That's some Zulu stuff right
there.
I'm glad you're here.

308
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:14,800
First one for World.

309
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:17,400
(CHEERING, LAUGHING)

310
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:20,320
Alright, Rob,
what do you want to choose?

311
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:29,240
LUKE: Oh, he's gone for the box.
Oh, yes! Mystery box.

312
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:32,360
Alright. It's a mystery.

313
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,640
Nice.

314
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,480
CIRIE: No, as long as we keep it
out of their hands, it's good.

315
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,760
Ooh, interesting.

316
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:43,800
What'll we do with it?

317
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:46,200
Alright, here we go. Next round.

318
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,840
JANINE: Come on, budgie
smugglers!

319
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:52,400
We have Tommi for World
taking on George for Australia.

320
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:56,640
Are you good at sports?
No. Terrible.

321
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:58,320
Survivors ready?

322
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,440
Go!

323
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,480
SHONEE: Oh, my God!
George gets the jump!

324
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:03,920
Oh!
(ONLOOKERS EXCLAIM)

325
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:05,840
Holy moly!

326
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:08,640
Tommi takes
a hard hit on the neck.

327
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:11,880
He dusts himself off,
gets to the bags first.

328
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,000
Struggling to connect.
Oh!

329
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,600
Oh, my God!

330
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:18,080
Yah!
(DING!)

331
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,200
Yeah!
That's it!

332
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,440
George does it for Australia.

333
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,600
Georgie boy!
Yes, baby!

334
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:24,960
Whoo!

335
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,520
George is a beast, man.

336
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,600
I think I
am going to take the flint

337
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:32,000
and make our life
a little bit easier.

338
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,560
Yeah. There you go.

339
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:35,320
SARAH: Well done, Georgie.

340
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,800
One-nil for challenges.
Who would have thought?

341
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,720
Alright. Australia,
who are you putting up?

342
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,400
Alright. Kirby.

343
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:46,760
World?
PARVATI: Should I go?

344
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,120
OK. I'll go.

345
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:50,160
Parvati.
I ain't scared of Kirby.

346
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,760
(LAUGHS)
Come on up.

347
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:55,080
The baby.
Yeah.

348
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:57,840
Alright. Survivors ready?

349
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:00,720
Go!

350
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,480
GEORGE: Go, Kirby!

351
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,800
Neck and neck down the slides.

352
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,840
TONY: Go, go, go, go!
CIRIE: Go!

353
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,240
Nice, nice.
You there, you there!

354
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:12,320
You got it, you got it.
Parvati with a slight lead.

355
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,920
Is this going to help her?
Oh! (BLEEP)

356
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,400
Kirby gets there last.

357
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,960
(DING!)
But she takes it out!

358
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,720
(CHEERING)
Yeah, Kirby!

359
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,440
Takes the fruit basket.

360
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,280
They could be hungry after that.

361
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,640
Alright.
We have Tony for World...

362
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,600
We got to try to look like
these guys, man.

363
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,480
Yeah. So anyways...
(BABBLES NONSENSE, LAUGHS)

364
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,120
..taking on Luke for Australia.

365
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:38,120
Go!

366
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:40,040
(ONLOOKERS SHOUT SUPPORT)

367
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,320
Luke gets the jump.

368
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,680
Off the slide first.

369
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:45,160
DAVID: Go get it, get it,
get it, get it.

370
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,880
Come on, Tony!
(DING!)

371
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,640
And that is it!
(AUSSIES CHEERING)

372
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:50,040
We'll take the tarp.

373
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:52,680
We're gonna be dry! Yeah!
Whoo!

374
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:56,080
Alright. Survivors ready? Go!

375
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:57,720
GEORGE: Go, Sarah!
PARVATI: Let's go, Cirie!

376
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,640
We have Sarah for Australia
taking on Cirie for World.

377
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,880
(DING!)

378
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,080
(ALL CHEER)

379
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,440
Alright.
This is what we're taking.

380
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:08,400
Cirie taking the comfort item.

381
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:11,560
GEORGE: Yeah. Nothing like
a woollen blanket in Samoa.

382
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:13,040
We are watching you.

383
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,480
(LAUGHS)

384
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,080
Survivors ready? Go!

385
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:17,720
(ONLOOKERS SHOUT SUPPORT)

386
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:20,920
Kass for World
taking on Janine for Australia.

387
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,720
GEORGE: Look at that transition.
Go, Janine!

388
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,880
(DING!)
(WORLD CHEERS)

389
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,240
Kass does it!

390
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,840
Oh, I'd love a tea!

391
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:31,800
Going to go with
the coffee and tea.
Yeah!

392
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:36,640
Here we go. Final round.

393
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:40,920
Lisa for World
taking on Shonee for Australia.

394
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,160
OK, I'm ready.

395
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:45,480
Shonee, the most important
reward is still left
on the shelf.

396
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:47,720
Come on, Lisa!
Do it for the bubbly.

397
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,480
How much do you like champagne?

398
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,440
So much. What about y...
I know you do.

399
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:52,680
I love it.

400
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,320
Survivors ready?

401
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:57,520
JANINE: Come on, Shon! (CLAPS)
You got this.

402
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:58,600
Go!

403
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,080
(ONLOOKERS SHOUT SUPPORT)

404
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,280
Lisa gets the jump.

405
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,800
(SQUEALS)

406
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,200
TONY: There you go!
Go, go, go, go, go!

407
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,680
Shonee desperately trying
to close it down.

408
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,120
Quick under the net.

409
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:10,440
She gets to the bags first.

410
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,240
Can she close this out?

411
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,680
Oh!
She misses.

412
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:15,840
Lisa going for the win.

413
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,840
(DING!)
(ALL CHEER)

414
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:20,200
And Lisa does it for World!

415
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,160
ROB: Was that one throw?

416
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,600
Insane. That was one throw?

417
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,240
That is it.
TONY: That's all you need.

418
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:28,720
Good effort, Shon.
So unlucky when you can't throw.

419
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:29,880
Well done.
(LAUGHS)

420
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,880
Good job! (LAUGHS)

421
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,680
One throw?! Are you kidding me?

422
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,040
Alright, everyone.

423
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:38,480
Head out to your new camps,
and good luck.

424
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,480
GEORGE: Let's go!
Let's get this game started.

425
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,240
TONY: We only have 16 days.

426
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,760
This is going to be
fast and furious.

427
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,560
This is gonna be scrambling,

428
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:47,920
building alliances,

429
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,400
talking about
who's gonna go home.

430
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,720
I don't think the fans know
what this is gonna be about,

431
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:53,840
how fast this is gonna move.

432
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:56,040
Their heads
are gonna be spinning.

433
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,520
TONY: Home sweet home.

434
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,760
CIRIE: Oh, my God,
it's beautiful.
ROB: Whoo!

435
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,640
Wow.

436
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:31,520
Australia versus the World
is going to be the showdown
of the century.

437
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,600
Buckle up, kids.

438
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:37,320
This is a 16-day game with
the best from around the world.

439
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:40,560
This is, like, juiced-up
Survivor to the extreme.

440
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:41,560
Home sweet home.

441
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:49,400
Oh, so we can't
even open the box?

442
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,640
Maybe there's a key in...

443
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,720
This key could be anywhere.

444
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,800
And we've won two bottles
of champagne.

445
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:03,240
To me, there's
an obvious place to start.

446
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:05,520
Well done, guys.
(OTHERS CHEER)

447
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:07,840
In a game that's
as fast as this one,

448
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:10,920
relationships are gonna
have to solidify really fast.

449
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,000
The World!
ALL: Cheers!

450
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,960
What do you say?

451
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,240
Kippis?
(LAUGHS) Yeah.

452
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:17,720
Kippis!
Cheers.

453
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:18,920
Cheers!

454
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:22,880
So, do we want to just
officially introduce ourselves

455
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,640
and where we're from?
Yeah, of course.

456
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:26,160
Oh, OK, then I'll start.

457
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:27,200
I'm Cirie.

458
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,640
Obviously, I'm from
the United States.

459
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:31,880
OK? (LAUGHS) Next?
OK.

460
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:34,120
Nice to meet you.
Thanks for sharing.

461
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:36,200
My name is Tony.
I'm from the USA.

462
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,640
There does seem to be

463
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:41,440
seven individuals
meeting each other out here.

464
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:43,400
So, I'm Rob.
I'm from South Africa.

465
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,280
It's my second time
playing Survivor.

466
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:49,200
But there's four internationals
and three Americans out here.

467
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,520
My name is Lisa
and I live in New Zealand.

468
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:54,840
My name is Kass
and I played Survivor Quebec.

469
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,280
Tommi. Played two years ago.

470
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:58,600
I lost by one vote.

471
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,440
(OTHERS EXCLAIM)
Yeah.

472
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:03,360
We have to stay US strong
until merge.

473
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:07,440
Alright.
So, bamboo, palm fronds.

474
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:09,200
OK, off we go.

475
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:18,120
Oh, look at you
taking the big ones, eh?

476
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:20,160
I've been lifting weights,
you know?
(CHUCKLES)

477
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:22,960
To prepare. I gotta get my muscles
big as yours so I can compete.

478
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:26,600
But the thing is,
Tony's a loose cannon.

479
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:28,880
I don't know about Tony.

480
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,960
Is he gonna trust me? Is he gonna
want to work with me?

481
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,840
I need to talk to you
about you and me.

482
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:34,360
OK.
Because I feel like...

483
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:36,600
I'm a little bit nervous.
You shouldn't be.

484
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,520
What I'm nervous about is...

485
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:40,200
(QUIETER) What I'm nervous about
is three of us.

486
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:41,440
Oh, yeah.

487
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:45,280
That's what I'm nervous about.
But it could be good.

488
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:48,160
Well, perception.
If we pull in...

489
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,480
Percep... Perception.

490
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:50,640
Yeah.

491
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:55,000
But I've got Cirie out here.

492
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:58,600
It's been over 15 years
since we've played together,

493
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:00,840
but that's my girl.
I love Cirie.

494
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:03,880
She talks out of the side of her
mouth when she's strategising.

495
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:05,600
(LAUGHS) It's the best.

496
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:14,800
I think you, me and Tony should
try to keep each other safe
till merge.

497
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,080
I agree.

498
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:17,880
OK. I'm not gonna hang out
with you very much.

499
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:19,520
Yeah. Me either. Alright.

500
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:25,800
Parvati and I go WAY back,
to Micronesia. (LAUGHS)

501
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:31,320
We had an all-girls alliance
called the Black Widow Brigade,

502
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:32,960
and it worked flawlessly.

503
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:35,000
We're spinning the guys around
as much as we can

504
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,640
till they don't know
which way is up,

505
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:40,160
and then we're devouring them
one at a time.

506
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:42,960
Nat, tell them that if he
were to give you the necklace,

507
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:45,920
that would redeem him
and we would vote for Amanda.

508
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:47,000
Who would fall for that?

509
00:25:48,040 --> 00:25:49,960
I want to give individual
immunity to Natalie.

510
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:56,520
You officially go down as
the dumbest Survivor ever.

511
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:59,360
And then Parv went on
to win that season.

512
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:02,120
MY season.
That I SHOULD have won.

513
00:26:02,120 --> 00:26:03,760
(LAUGHS)

514
00:26:05,360 --> 00:26:07,840
Now, us, the Americans,

515
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:10,040
we walked in
with a huge target on our back,

516
00:26:10,040 --> 00:26:13,680
so I can see
maybe something happening

517
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:15,720
with the other World tribe
members

518
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:17,320
that are not from the US.

519
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:22,040
And you can't help but notice
Rob off having conversations.

520
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,040
The Americans, yeah.

521
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:30,080
Yes.

522
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:37,960
Really?

523
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:46,720
Listen, guys, if the Americans
take one of us out,

524
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:48,000
they will dominate this tribe.

525
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Yeah.

526
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:05,360
LISA: I've been a fan of Survivor
since the very first episode.

527
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,440
I love it so much.

528
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,720
When there was
a New Zealand version,

529
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:10,720
I just thought,
"I can never go on Survivor."

530
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:12,200
Like, "What?" Like, "Me?"

531
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:15,400
And I did it. (LAUGHS) I did it.

532
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:18,240
I won the very first time
I played Survivor.

533
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:21,640
So few people get to live out
their dream in life once,

534
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,360
and I'm getting to do it twice.

535
00:27:27,200 --> 00:27:28,360
Me?
Yeah. (LAUGHS)

536
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:31,000
Yeah.

537
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,360
I think we all are. Yeah, yeah.

538
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:35,920
Like, talk about lifelong dreams
coming true.

539
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:40,760
Being able to meet
frickin' Cirie Fields.

540
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:45,800
If you're watching this now
and you don't understand,

541
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:47,160
like, go and watch
some more Survivor.

542
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:49,520
Go and watch
all of Cirie's seasons

543
00:27:49,520 --> 00:27:51,360
and come back to me and say,

544
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:53,040
"Oh, I'm really sorry, Lisa.
You were right."

545
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,440
Yeah.

546
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:56,640
Um...

547
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:00,640
Uh-huh?
But...

548
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:02,560
..like everyone in the world,

549
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:04,320
you're my favourite Survivor
player, right?

550
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,480
Aw! Thank you.

551
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:09,440
I'll never go against you.
I know. But listen...

552
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:11,080
Do you know, this is going to be
fast and furious,

553
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:12,880
and I know New Zealanders
are laid back.

554
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:18,040
I don't have any allegiance
to anybody here.

555
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:19,600
I will never turn against you.

556
00:28:19,600 --> 00:28:22,160
Look at me in the eyes
so you know.

557
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:25,720
But I have no desire
to ever turn against you.

558
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:27,880
I would love to play this game
with you.

559
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,960
Especially if we can
make it to the merge

560
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:32,240
and kind of get
with the Australians
and see what happens.

561
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:37,440
The non-US players -
Rob, Kass, Tommi and I -

562
00:28:37,440 --> 00:28:39,920
are really trying
to build a nice alliance,

563
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:42,120
a very sensible alliance,

564
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:45,800
but now maybe Cirie and I
have something too.

565
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:48,440
Ridiculous that I can say
Cirie and I have something.

566
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,560
Just ridiculous!

567
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:53,320
There's huge targets here,
and we're not one of them. So...

568
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:56,800
If I had to, like, choose...
Don't know what to do.

569
00:28:56,800 --> 00:29:00,040
This is the worst position
anyone playing Survivor
has ever been put at.

570
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:18,320
LUKE: Alright, alright.

571
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:20,440
Mad, huh?

572
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,440
GEORGE: Wow!

573
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:24,120
SARAH: How cool's this?
It's beautiful.

574
00:29:24,120 --> 00:29:25,400
JANINE: Oh, my God.

575
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:26,560
Heya!

576
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:28,120
Oh, here's our stuff.

577
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:29,520
Home sweet home.

578
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:33,040
(CHUCKLES)

579
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:34,760
Here we are.
(OTHERS EXCLAIM)

580
00:29:34,760 --> 00:29:36,160
Amazing.

581
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:40,000
Here I am, looking around at
the rest of this Aussie tribe.

582
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,640
They are the best of the best.

583
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:46,600
Am I legitimately worried?

584
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:48,600
Yes, I am.

585
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:50,080
I've got a big problem here.

586
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:52,520
So, who has played together
before?

587
00:29:52,520 --> 00:29:54,320
What are... what are the combos
we're working with?

588
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,600
Aren't you a superfan, Sarah?

589
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:58,200
I know, I know. I just want
to... I want it out in the open.

590
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:03,040
I don't have
the pre-existing relationships

591
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:06,000
that people like David and Luke
have on this tribe.

592
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,440
(BOTH LAUGH)

593
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:17,960
The only relationship that I
have on this tribe is Shonee.

594
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,120
But she's got an axe to grind
against me

595
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:21,520
because I voted her out

596
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:23,360
the last time we were both here
on this island.

597
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:37,440
So the first thing I need to do
is clear the air with Shonee.

598
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:40,840
Because if I reunite
the Spice Girls,

599
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:42,320
we'll be able to work together.

600
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:43,680
And Shonee and George

601
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:47,080
is a very dangerous and fun
combination in this game.

602
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:57,080
Yeah, I've been good. Yeah,
just chilling. What about you?

603
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:59,880
Well, here's what I would
like to tell you, Shon.

604
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:00,960
Mm-hm?

605
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:04,600
I have absolutely no animosity
towards you...

606
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,960
..and I hope the feeling is
mutual!

607
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:09,400
(LAUGHS)
Yeah.

608
00:31:11,240 --> 00:31:14,880
I swear to God, Shon,
I'm looking around and going,

609
00:31:14,880 --> 00:31:17,440
"The only person
that I've played with

610
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:19,680
"and have a connection with..."
is you.

611
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:22,080
When it's good,
it's really good.

612
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:23,200
And do you know
what I tell myself?

613
00:31:23,200 --> 00:31:24,360
And when it's bad,
it's really bad.

614
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:26,960
When it's bad, it's bad, but it
took 34 days to get bad
last time.

615
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,600
We're only here for 16.
This is only 16.

616
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:31,840
So I'm just like... It looks
like it's going to be peaking
right then

617
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:34,320
and it's going to be
in the good spot. (CHUCKLES)

618
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:36,920
So you would legitimately
want to work with me?

619
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:39,480
I would think that's
a very exciting alliance.

620
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,520
Mmm.
I definitely would.

621
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:42,200
It does make sense.

622
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:44,440
It makes sense because...

623
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:47,200
..we'd kind of protect each other
until merge.

624
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:55,120
I don't want to work with George
under any circumstances.

625
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:58,640
I really appreciate it, Shon.
I really do.

626
00:31:58,640 --> 00:31:59,920
Yeah, it's good.

627
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,040
Red flag number one -

628
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:04,800
George has written a book
about manipulation.

629
00:32:04,800 --> 00:32:06,760
I have been a victim of that.

630
00:32:06,760 --> 00:32:12,360
But I do not have pre-existing
relationships on this tribe

631
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:14,200
other than George.

632
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:18,160
Getting nowhere.
Do you know what?

633
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,440
None of youse care.

634
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:20,800
Ooh!

635
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:28,640
Coming into this game,
I need to lower my threat level.

636
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:30,960
And that's why
I'm not going to have

637
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:35,120
any sort of public
ride-or-die relationships.

638
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:37,480
Things need to be kept in
secret.

639
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:38,480
How are you feeling?

640
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:39,640
Yeah, I was gonna ask you
the same.

641
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:41,600
How are you? Where are you at?

642
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,320
Well...

643
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:46,800
OK.
Yeah.

644
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:48,400
(LAUGHS) Why?

645
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:52,640
Well, I think that, like,
obviously, you and I
have a clean slate.

646
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:56,560
There's no bad blood straight
out of the gate,
you know what I mean?

647
00:32:56,560 --> 00:32:59,280
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I just feel like
it could be good.

648
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:02,520
Do we make us a secret,
solid alliance?

649
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:03,680
Yes.
And that way,

650
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:05,280
we can just sort of
keep an eye out.

651
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:07,160
Mmm. Yes.
Yeah.

652
00:33:07,160 --> 00:33:08,160
Yeah, yeah.

653
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:09,440
Yeah.

654
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:15,800
Yeah, I'm...

655
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:21,000
I'm not in Samoa for the great
weather or the fine dining.

656
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:24,040
I am here
because I want revenge.

657
00:33:25,080 --> 00:33:29,000
And I have one name on my list
now, and that's George.

658
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:31,840
Dad bod is in.
Mm-hm.

659
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:36,000
This is my victory tour.
It's going to be iconic.

660
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:38,200
I-Shon-ic. (LAUGHS)

661
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:49,360
GEORGE: I feel happy.
I'm happy I'm back.

662
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:50,400
Me too.

663
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:53,040
Do you know what I'm thinking?
The water. Do you want to go.

664
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:56,040
Who's keen for a dip?
An ocean dip.

665
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:59,320
I've still got some...
(LAUGHTER)

666
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:02,160
Sorry, guys. There's only
so many hours in the day.

667
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:03,160
You know.

668
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:12,920
I really feel like I was
born to play this game.

669
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:16,520
Being back here,
it just feels, like, natural.

670
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:18,440
This game is in my DNA.

671
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:21,520
I've already
played with half of these guys.

672
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:23,920
How are you doing?
Yeah. Good.

673
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:27,120
We're good, I'm good.
Yeah. 100%.

674
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:31,560
But I'm the only winner
on the Australian tribe,

675
00:34:31,560 --> 00:34:33,880
so I feel like
I'm pretty exposed out here.

676
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:37,480
So for me, the only
thing to do is play bigger.

677
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:38,520
So immediately off the bat,

678
00:34:38,520 --> 00:34:43,080
I'm looking in the fruit basket
searching for idols.

679
00:34:46,520 --> 00:34:49,720
I spoke to South African Rob
openly at the challenge today.

680
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,760
It's like the Olympics
of Survivor, right?

681
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,320
Lucky I'm Usain Bolt.

682
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:58,280
You don't want to be the Raygun
of the Australian Olympic team.

683
00:35:01,520 --> 00:35:02,920
That's kind of George.

684
00:35:04,680 --> 00:35:05,960
OK. Open it.

685
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:08,600
Oh, wow. This is huge.

686
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:10,480
Dude, this is...
How big this is.

687
00:35:10,480 --> 00:35:11,800
Huge.

688
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,400
Are you trying
to steal my best friend?

689
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:17,800
What's going on here?
I'm George from Bankstown.

690
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:19,840
Lovely to finally meet you.

691
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:21,720
Yeah. I'm good, I'm good.

692
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:24,200
I know George might be
the strategy genius,

693
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:26,520
but he's someone
that has always felt like

694
00:35:26,520 --> 00:35:29,040
he has to live up
to my shadow strategically.

695
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:31,080
Not everyone wants
to live up to perfection.

696
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:33,160
It's tricky,

697
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:36,520
but he's also
a huge target.

698
00:35:36,520 --> 00:35:38,880
That's very useful
for someone like me,

699
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:41,280
who is clearly the number one
target in this game.

700
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,320
How are you doing?
I'm doing good.

701
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:47,560
What are we doing?
What are we doing?

702
00:35:47,560 --> 00:35:48,600
Yeah, let's just get into it.

703
00:35:48,600 --> 00:35:51,360
Honestly, I'd love to work with
you and Luke

704
00:35:51,360 --> 00:35:54,640
and be the buffer that protects us
and propels us forward.

705
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:56,000
But we're all shields
to each other.

706
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:57,560
That's why I call it
the buffer strategy.

707
00:35:59,160 --> 00:36:01,600
So, I'll be I'll be super honest
and open with you right now.

708
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,040
I'm not voting you
off no matter what.

709
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:05,920
I just can't.
I worry about you after merge,

710
00:36:05,920 --> 00:36:07,560
because after merge,
I'm in big trouble.

711
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:09,640
He's in really big trouble.
You shouldn't.

712
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:11,440
You've got some people
that just don't have

713
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:13,800
the same reputation in the game
that the king of the jungle,

714
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:16,480
the Golden God
and the King of Bankstown have.

715
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:17,920
You know?

716
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:19,800
(LAUGHTER)

717
00:36:21,440 --> 00:36:23,280
Would this not be
the best alliance ever?

718
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:26,240
Like, seriously, one of the most
exciting alliances ever.

719
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:27,520
It would be good.
Ever.

720
00:36:27,520 --> 00:36:29,560
It would be pretty good.
It'll break the internet.

721
00:36:29,560 --> 00:36:31,040
Yeah.

722
00:36:31,040 --> 00:36:32,920
Oh...

723
00:36:34,040 --> 00:36:35,600
What are we calling ourselves?

724
00:36:38,440 --> 00:36:40,600
If you want to call our alliance
the Power Bottoms,

725
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:41,960
I'm all for it, David.

726
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:44,320
(LAUGHTER)

727
00:36:44,320 --> 00:36:46,400
I'm just humouring George.

728
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,920
Yeah, the boys are on the bottom,
so we're the power bottom.

729
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,200
Alright.

730
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,760
He might be
a bit of a strategic master,

731
00:36:56,760 --> 00:36:58,600
but he has got
zero self-awareness

732
00:36:58,600 --> 00:37:00,200
in comparing his game to mine.

733
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:01,840
Like, George,
you have never won, dude.

734
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:04,320
And you're trying to tell me
you can be a shield for me.

735
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:06,240
OK, bubby. OK.

736
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:24,080
Yeah.
(LAUGHTER)

737
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:39,320
I bet you we'll get this fire
before they do with the flint.

738
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:40,520
I bet you.

739
00:37:42,040 --> 00:37:44,080
Cheers.
Yeah.

740
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:45,680
Rob is a fire guy.

741
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:49,280
Go. Go as fast as you can.
OK. Yeah.

742
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:50,600
Like that.
Like that?

743
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,080
We should have something now, man.

744
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:58,520
Alright, look,
I'm giving up here.

745
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,600
I've played Survivor
five times now,

746
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:09,800
and I know this game is less
about surviving the elements,

747
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:11,240
and it's more
about surviving each other.

748
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:14,080
How close are Aussies
and New Zealand in general?

749
00:38:14,080 --> 00:38:16,840
Oh, it's a bit of a like...

750
00:38:16,840 --> 00:38:20,160
Like Finland and Sweden.
You tell me. Maybe.

751
00:38:22,040 --> 00:38:24,480
There are four players from
the world

752
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:27,240
and three players
from the United States.

753
00:38:27,240 --> 00:38:29,520
So I don't
want to make it too obvious

754
00:38:29,520 --> 00:38:32,720
that I'm working with Cirie
to bring in some other people.

755
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:40,200
Your shirt is gonna be like...
Yeah.

756
00:38:40,200 --> 00:38:42,000
It's, like, the most dangerous
thing you could touch.

757
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:44,040
OK, I'm gonna stick with you.

758
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:47,480
I feel like
you've got the survivalism.

759
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:50,960
My plan is to go
head over to South Africa

760
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:53,360
and talk to the Zulu king.

761
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:55,640
I tend to eat guys like Rob
for breakfast,

762
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:58,080
but Rob gives me options.

763
00:38:58,080 --> 00:39:01,680
So, I want to get him on my side
as quickly as I possibly can.

764
00:39:01,680 --> 00:39:03,720
I need Rob magnetised to me.

765
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:05,040
These are the ones.

766
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:09,560
The only people I know
are Cirie and Tony.

767
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:11,880
Yeah, that's what I mean.

768
00:39:13,520 --> 00:39:16,680
How are things? I don't know.
Fine, I guess.

769
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:27,800
Yours are beautiful. Stop!
You're doing that to me.

770
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:32,080
The web weaving has begun.

771
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:37,800
And I'm, like, three steps ahead.

772
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:40,200
I saw Rob and David
clicking at the challenge.

773
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:44,120
I know David from another show,

774
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:46,320
so I'm thinking
I can use this David connection

775
00:39:46,320 --> 00:39:48,440
to build a bridge with Rob maybe.

776
00:39:53,120 --> 00:39:56,560
I haven't seen South African
Survivor, but I know who you are.

777
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:58,240
How?

778
00:39:58,240 --> 00:40:00,440
Because David loves you.

779
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:02,160
David?
David on the other side.

780
00:40:02,160 --> 00:40:03,160
How do you know that?

781
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:05,840
Because David and I
played a game together.

782
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:09,440
Big secret.

783
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:13,480
You guys just got off
another show?

784
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:15,920
Yeah. Cannot tell anyone this.
Yeah. Of course.

785
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:21,400
OK. It's called
Deal or No Deal Island.

786
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:24,920
He loves you.
He wants to play with you.

787
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,640
I can see.
You can tell.

788
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:28,000
Yeah. Yeah.
Yeah.

789
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,560
I would like to play with him
too.

790
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:37,200
So, I think the stronger, bigger
threats going into merge

791
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:40,320
is probably an important thing
to keep together.

792
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:43,400
Yeah.
But keep that between us, please.

793
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:52,040
I promise.
That's how you can trust me.

794
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,480
Yes, exactly.
That's actually a perfect way.

795
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:56,120
You just gave me something
I can prove to you.

796
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:03,320
I am working with Rob
and working Rob simultaneously.

797
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:05,760
I'm still the Black Widow.

798
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:09,200
And I'll still wrap you up
in my web and suck your blood.

799
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:14,520
Yeah, that's what I'm hoping.

800
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:26,880
ROB: Part of Parvati's gameplay
is to be flirtatious.

801
00:41:28,960 --> 00:41:32,960
But Parvati, nah. Sorry, boss.
Not gonna work here.

802
00:41:37,240 --> 00:41:41,680
We've got a solid four -
Tommi, Kass, Lisa and myself.

803
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:43,200
Literally all you need
in this game.

804
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,480
We're the only people
who are alone here.

805
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:48,560
You've got seven horses
for Australia.

806
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:49,560
Yeah.

807
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:51,560
You've got three horses
for America.

808
00:41:51,560 --> 00:41:54,120
Our countries
have one horse in this race.

809
00:41:54,120 --> 00:41:57,320
One of us leaves
the Americans tear us to pieces.

810
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:04,360
I can promise you one thing.

811
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:08,680
An American will go home first
from the World tribe.

812
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:15,040
That is a promise that I promise you
I will not break.

813
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:17,960
Sorry. Not sorry.

814
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:43,800
Day Two. And it's my birthday.

815
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:46,480
I don't think I've ever celebrated
a birthday on Survivor.

816
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:49,440
This is a first for me.
Out of five seasons.

817
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:50,440
Oh.

818
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:53,440
Thanks, guys.

819
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:56,440
She said all she wants for her
birthday is an immunity win.

820
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:59,800
One immunity. Can we deliver?
Yeah. We can.

821
00:43:04,160 --> 00:43:06,720
If I stay in this game tonight,
I am tied

822
00:43:06,720 --> 00:43:10,240
for the most amount of days
played for Survivor ever.

823
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:12,240
152, with my boy Boston Rob.

824
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:14,520
And I'm coming for that record.

825
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:20,160
Yeah. This is not
the Australian side.

826
00:43:20,160 --> 00:43:22,720
They would do it just
because it is your birthday.

827
00:43:46,800 --> 00:43:47,840
Come on in.

828
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:03,720
Hello.
Hello.

829
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:09,400
So, Cirie.

830
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:11,800
How were your first 24 hours
on the beach?

831
00:44:11,800 --> 00:44:13,600
Fabulous. Wonderful.

832
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:15,960
We enjoyed
getting to know each other

833
00:44:15,960 --> 00:44:18,320
over a couple glasses
of champagne.

834
00:44:18,320 --> 00:44:20,200
Relax. Chill.

835
00:44:20,200 --> 00:44:22,200
Parvati,
you've played a lot of Survivor.

836
00:44:22,200 --> 00:44:25,960
Does this feel like business as usual
or is this a whole other ball game?

837
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:28,040
I think
the more Survivor you play,

838
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:30,160
the less you care about surviving.

839
00:44:30,160 --> 00:44:31,760
(LAUGHTER)

840
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:36,680
Did you get fire?
We had so much fire.

841
00:44:36,680 --> 00:44:38,120
It was so hot.

842
00:44:38,120 --> 00:44:40,600
Alright. OK. So, George,

843
00:44:40,600 --> 00:44:43,480
do you think they've managed
to open that mystery box?

844
00:44:43,480 --> 00:44:46,080
Who knows what's in the box?
Tell us.

845
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:47,480
Yeah, tell us what's in the box.

846
00:44:49,720 --> 00:44:52,240
Alright. Shall we get to it?
ALL: Oh, yeah.

847
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:54,640
Alright. For today's challenge,

848
00:44:54,640 --> 00:44:57,600
you're going to work together
to move a heavy staircase

849
00:44:57,600 --> 00:44:59,640
and use it to climb over a wall.

850
00:44:59,640 --> 00:45:01,120
You'll then use giant blocks

851
00:45:01,120 --> 00:45:03,560
to build another staircase

852
00:45:03,560 --> 00:45:05,080
to reach the top of the tower.

853
00:45:06,760 --> 00:45:08,880
Finally, two of you
will use a slingshot

854
00:45:08,880 --> 00:45:11,680
to fire coconuts
at a series of targets.

855
00:45:13,160 --> 00:45:16,200
The first tribe to smash
all their targets wins immunity.

856
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:17,760
And this...

857
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:24,520
..is the immunity idol.

858
00:45:28,800 --> 00:45:32,360
This is what you want. With this
back at camp, you are safe.

859
00:45:32,360 --> 00:45:35,160
Guaranteed another day
in the game.

860
00:45:35,160 --> 00:45:37,360
Without it, you're going to be
seeing me at Tribal Council,

861
00:45:37,360 --> 00:45:40,520
where one of you will become
the first person voted out of

862
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:42,560
Australia Versus the World.

863
00:45:42,560 --> 00:45:43,840
No-one wants to be that person.

864
00:45:43,840 --> 00:45:45,680
GEORGE: No.

865
00:45:45,680 --> 00:45:48,120
Alright, I'll give you
a minute to strategise.

866
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:49,480
Let's get to it.

867
00:45:59,920 --> 00:46:03,440
Alright, here we go for immunity.

868
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:05,160
Survivors, ready?

869
00:46:06,760 --> 00:46:08,160
Go!

870
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:11,160
Go! Go that way.
That staircase is a beast.

871
00:46:11,160 --> 00:46:13,680
Three, two, one.
Come on, guys.

872
00:46:18,680 --> 00:46:19,880
Push it, push it! Go, go!

873
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:22,120
Wow! World tribe
quick out of the gate!

874
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:23,760
Nice.

875
00:46:23,760 --> 00:46:26,240
Almost there, almost there,
almost there.

876
00:46:26,240 --> 00:46:27,560
They're at the wall.

877
00:46:27,560 --> 00:46:30,000
Now everyone's got to go
over the top.

878
00:46:32,320 --> 00:46:35,120
Come on, Aussies,
you're falling behind. Let's go.

879
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:38,400
Come on! Let's go, Aussie!
Go!

880
00:46:38,400 --> 00:46:40,400
There you are.
Now you're at the wall.

881
00:46:40,400 --> 00:46:41,840
Go! Go!

882
00:46:42,840 --> 00:46:45,080
World tribe almost over.

883
00:46:45,080 --> 00:46:47,800
Aussies trying to close the gap.

884
00:46:47,800 --> 00:46:51,240
Tony last to go over
for World tribe.

885
00:46:51,240 --> 00:46:52,240
Thanks.

886
00:46:52,240 --> 00:46:53,800
Looks good. Go, World.

887
00:46:55,520 --> 00:46:56,680
Now you've got six giant blocks.

888
00:46:56,680 --> 00:47:00,520
You need to wrestle them into
position and build another staircase.

889
00:47:00,520 --> 00:47:02,840
OK. Now slack.
Not working, not working.

890
00:47:02,840 --> 00:47:04,200
Keep flipping it.

891
00:47:04,200 --> 00:47:06,000
Flip it. Flip it.
It's fine.

892
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:07,720
Go, DJ.
Go, Aussies!

893
00:47:09,240 --> 00:47:10,760
David's over. You're good.

894
00:47:10,760 --> 00:47:12,240
Go, Australia! Let's go.

895
00:47:12,240 --> 00:47:14,880
Someone be the brains!
Get this up the right way.

896
00:47:14,880 --> 00:47:16,640
Is this the right side?
No, no! Stop! Stop, stop!

897
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:18,160
It's gonna spin twice.

898
00:47:18,160 --> 00:47:19,480
Closer?

899
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:21,840
Not only do you have to have
your blocks in position,

900
00:47:21,840 --> 00:47:24,520
but they need to be
the correct orientation.

901
00:47:24,520 --> 00:47:25,960
Fingers clear.

902
00:47:25,960 --> 00:47:28,560
The symbols need to be
the right way up.

903
00:47:28,560 --> 00:47:29,640
OK. Again, again.

904
00:47:29,640 --> 00:47:32,320
Aussies have their first block
in position.

905
00:47:32,320 --> 00:47:33,720
Working on their seconds.

906
00:47:33,720 --> 00:47:36,720
Let's go. Shon, we're gonna do this
box this time. Go.

907
00:47:36,720 --> 00:47:38,960
Go back. Go back, go back!

908
00:47:38,960 --> 00:47:41,160
World have their first block
in position.

909
00:47:41,160 --> 00:47:42,200
That way?

910
00:47:42,200 --> 00:47:44,680
Come this way.
No, it's on the floor.

911
00:47:44,680 --> 00:47:47,960
Yeah. No, but let's just straighten
it out. Let's just do a flip.

912
00:47:47,960 --> 00:47:49,160
Aussies slowing down.

913
00:47:49,160 --> 00:47:53,480
Meanwhile, World tribe,
a well-oiled machine.

914
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:54,840
Here we go.

915
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:58,120
Lower, lower, lower.
We're almost there.

916
00:47:58,120 --> 00:47:59,400
Lower, lower.

917
00:47:59,400 --> 00:48:02,000
Perfect.
World now have three in position.

918
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:05,160
First row is the easy one.
Now it gets tricky.

919
00:48:05,160 --> 00:48:06,440
Now.
One more.

920
00:48:06,440 --> 00:48:09,800
It's gonna spin twice
when you get to there. Closer.

921
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:14,520
Now you've got to get those giant
blocks on top of that first row.

922
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:16,640
The mouth facing to the floor.

923
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:19,080
There's two rows up. Alright?

924
00:48:19,080 --> 00:48:20,680
Push, push, push.

925
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:25,600
That's it.
Tony, Rob, Tommi.

926
00:48:25,600 --> 00:48:27,440
Getting that first one up.

927
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:30,160
Is it right?

928
00:48:31,280 --> 00:48:33,480
You just need
to slide it back into position.

929
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:34,720
That's it.

930
00:48:34,720 --> 00:48:36,840
Three. Two. One. Go, go!

931
00:48:36,840 --> 00:48:39,400
Aussies working on their second row.

932
00:48:39,400 --> 00:48:41,800
Gonna try the side approach.

933
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:42,840
Stop.

934
00:48:44,160 --> 00:48:48,200
David, Luke, George and Sarah
wrestle that next one up.

935
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:49,600
No, no, no, it's the wrong side.

936
00:48:49,600 --> 00:48:51,400
Yeah, but we can rotate it
from up there.

937
00:48:52,360 --> 00:48:55,720
Drop the box.
World have five blocks in position.

938
00:48:55,720 --> 00:48:58,280
That final block
is the most difficult.

939
00:48:58,280 --> 00:48:59,600
Come on, guys.

940
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:02,320
It's going to take a lot of effort
to get it all the way to the top.

941
00:49:02,320 --> 00:49:04,480
This box has to get up first.
Trust me.

942
00:49:04,480 --> 00:49:05,600
Leave it. It's fine.
It's fine.

943
00:49:05,600 --> 00:49:08,120
It has to get to the top.
No. This one.

944
00:49:08,120 --> 00:49:09,640
No. This one to the top.

945
00:49:09,640 --> 00:49:11,240
Once we have this,
we can't get to that.

946
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:12,520
Yes, that's what
I'm trying to say.

947
00:49:12,520 --> 00:49:16,400
World tribe's arguing. That opens
the window for the Aussie tribe.

948
00:49:17,400 --> 00:49:18,800
Good teamwork.
Watch fingers.

949
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:20,280
Teamwork, teamwork, teamwork.

950
00:49:20,280 --> 00:49:22,920
Slide, slide, slide!
Alright, baby, here we go.

951
00:49:22,920 --> 00:49:24,920
Same again.
Now we're back even.

952
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:25,920
Push.
We are back.

953
00:49:25,920 --> 00:49:28,160
Hold on, Dave.
Aussies down to their last block.

954
00:49:28,160 --> 00:49:29,360
We need to get this up.

955
00:49:29,360 --> 00:49:31,120
Hurry!
Three. Two. One. Go!

956
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:33,040
Both tribes
taking a different approach.

957
00:49:34,440 --> 00:49:36,320
Yeah. Stay under it.
Stay under it.

958
00:49:36,320 --> 00:49:38,960
We're there.
Pick it up.

959
00:49:38,960 --> 00:49:41,360
Whoa!
What's up?

960
00:49:41,360 --> 00:49:42,800
Almost losing it.

961
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:44,320
It's about to topple over.

962
00:49:46,880 --> 00:49:49,000
Here we go. Give me a gap.
I gotta get under.

963
00:49:49,000 --> 00:49:52,040
Yes, David. Get under, David.

964
00:49:54,240 --> 00:49:56,960
It's David going up,
using his back.

965
00:49:56,960 --> 00:49:58,800
Whoa!

966
00:49:58,800 --> 00:50:01,760
He's doing it all by himself.
That is crazy.

967
00:50:01,760 --> 00:50:03,200
(DAVID GRUNTS)

968
00:50:07,880 --> 00:50:09,320
Three, two, one, push.

969
00:50:12,360 --> 00:50:15,360
Deadlift.
What a beast the Golden God is!

970
00:50:15,360 --> 00:50:18,480
What an effort!
Aussies almost have it done.

971
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:20,640
(WORLD TRIBE ARGUES)

972
00:50:20,640 --> 00:50:21,640
Down. Down.

973
00:50:21,640 --> 00:50:23,680
Take this one!

974
00:50:23,680 --> 00:50:24,920
They did the same thing. Look.

975
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:27,960
And that is it.

976
00:50:27,960 --> 00:50:32,000
David and Luke get that final block
into position.

977
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:33,960
Go, go!
They're moving on.

978
00:50:35,720 --> 00:50:39,040
It's David on the slingshot first.

979
00:50:39,040 --> 00:50:40,040
Winds up.

980
00:50:42,400 --> 00:50:44,520
Goes long.

981
00:50:44,520 --> 00:50:46,640
Australia has a huge lead.

982
00:50:46,640 --> 00:50:50,120
It's going to give them plenty of
time to work out that slingshot.

983
00:50:50,120 --> 00:50:52,040
Are you ready? Are you ready?

984
00:50:52,040 --> 00:50:54,280
Rob underneath that final block.

985
00:50:54,280 --> 00:50:55,800
Taking the cue from Australia.

986
00:50:57,720 --> 00:50:58,760
Keep going.

987
00:51:01,440 --> 00:51:04,040
There it is. They get it up.

988
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:06,120
Good job.
Alright. Who's going up?

989
00:51:06,120 --> 00:51:07,680
Come on, Luke.

990
00:51:10,160 --> 00:51:13,000
Takes out the first target
for Australia.

991
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:15,720
Come on, let's go.
There it is. You're good, World.

992
00:51:15,720 --> 00:51:18,720
Let's go, let's go.
It's Rob and Tony.

993
00:51:18,720 --> 00:51:21,360
Keep passing them to me.
Going up for World.

994
00:51:21,360 --> 00:51:22,600
I need to...

995
00:51:22,600 --> 00:51:24,560
Come on, guys,
you can even it up.

996
00:51:26,560 --> 00:51:28,120
Slow down.

997
00:51:29,840 --> 00:51:31,960
(CHEERING)

998
00:51:31,960 --> 00:51:33,600
Australia gets another one.

999
00:51:34,680 --> 00:51:36,920
World still trying
to figure it out.

1000
00:51:36,920 --> 00:51:38,720
Desperate to close that gap.

1001
00:51:40,200 --> 00:51:41,840
Tony in now. He winds up.

1002
00:51:45,280 --> 00:51:47,280
Tony does it.
Do that again.

1003
00:51:49,400 --> 00:51:51,160
He connects again.

1004
00:51:51,160 --> 00:51:53,880
Oh, shit.
We are tied - two each.

1005
00:51:57,720 --> 00:51:59,280
Yeah.

1006
00:51:59,280 --> 00:52:00,280
David connects.

1007
00:52:00,280 --> 00:52:03,080
(PANEL SHATTERS)
Oh, my word!

1008
00:52:03,080 --> 00:52:04,280
And Luke connects.

1009
00:52:07,840 --> 00:52:09,480
World does it again.

1010
00:52:09,480 --> 00:52:11,280
Take your time, mate.

1011
00:52:13,480 --> 00:52:15,960
Yeah.
And again for Australia.

1012
00:52:17,880 --> 00:52:19,560
And another one.

1013
00:52:19,560 --> 00:52:22,080
Australia down to
their final two targets.

1014
00:52:22,080 --> 00:52:23,800
You can do it.

1015
00:52:25,160 --> 00:52:26,960
Tony does it.

1016
00:52:31,400 --> 00:52:34,120
(CHEERING)
Yes! One more!

1017
00:52:34,120 --> 00:52:36,600
Australia hit another target.

1018
00:52:36,600 --> 00:52:38,360
They're down
to their final target.

1019
00:52:38,360 --> 00:52:40,080
Come on. Come on.

1020
00:52:40,080 --> 00:52:44,040
David winding it up.
Going for the win.

1021
00:52:46,920 --> 00:52:48,240
(CHEERS)

1022
00:52:48,240 --> 00:52:51,280
David wins immunity for Australia.

1023
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:59,680
Bad luck, boys. Hey, bad luck.

1024
00:53:00,720 --> 00:53:02,280
Yeah.
It must be on your side.

1025
00:53:04,120 --> 00:53:05,760
It's quite serious
whatever's in there.

1026
00:53:05,760 --> 00:53:07,960
We'll find it. We'll find it.

1027
00:53:07,960 --> 00:53:09,400
Remember what we said, eh?

1028
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:11,240
Yeah, yeah. No, it's the start.
It's the start.

1029
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:15,600
He's asking for the key.

1030
00:53:19,160 --> 00:53:21,600
Australia, Congratulations.

1031
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:22,840
Immunity is yours.

1032
00:53:22,840 --> 00:53:24,800
(CHEERING)

1033
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:27,280
Aussies!

1034
00:53:29,240 --> 00:53:30,640
Let's go.

1035
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:33,160
Alright. You are safe.
Nobody going home.

1036
00:53:33,160 --> 00:53:34,800
Head back to camp.
Enjoy your night off.

1037
00:53:34,800 --> 00:53:37,080
Lead the way, Golden God.
Alright.

1038
00:53:38,520 --> 00:53:41,000
Look at this, you guys.
Pretty cool.

1039
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:42,080
Good luck, guys.

1040
00:53:42,080 --> 00:53:43,720
Thanks. Bye.

1041
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:45,320
Goodbye.
Bye, guys.

1042
00:53:47,480 --> 00:53:49,400
Alright, World,
Tribal Council tonight,

1043
00:53:49,400 --> 00:53:52,880
where one of you will become
the first person voted out.

1044
00:53:52,880 --> 00:53:55,320
Grab your gear. Head back
to camp. I'll see you tonight.

1045
00:54:03,760 --> 00:54:07,200
Losing the first
immunity challenge is terrible,

1046
00:54:07,200 --> 00:54:09,440
but we've got a solid four -

1047
00:54:09,440 --> 00:54:13,040
Tommi, Kass, Lisa and myself
against three Americans.

1048
00:54:13,040 --> 00:54:15,320
This is a very simple vote.

1049
00:54:15,320 --> 00:54:18,000
They call Cirie the greatest
player that's never won.

1050
00:54:18,000 --> 00:54:20,640
And sorry not sorry.
That's not changing today, boss.

1051
00:54:20,640 --> 00:54:22,840
(LAUGHS)

1052
00:54:37,560 --> 00:54:38,880
Worst case scenario.

1053
00:54:40,600 --> 00:54:44,000
Damn, man.
That was just brute strength.

1054
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:45,000
Yeah.

1055
00:54:49,280 --> 00:54:51,960
So, between
the four single countries,

1056
00:54:51,960 --> 00:54:53,960
Tommi, Lisa, Kass and myself.

1057
00:54:53,960 --> 00:54:56,080
This was discussed yesterday.

1058
00:54:56,080 --> 00:54:57,840
We stick together,
we take out an American.

1059
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:03,760
It's a very simple, easy vote.

1060
00:55:13,560 --> 00:55:16,960
I'm with the four, Parvati's
there and I decide, hey,

1061
00:55:16,960 --> 00:55:18,920
let me bring her in on this,

1062
00:55:18,920 --> 00:55:21,920
into the inner circle
of this alliance.

1063
00:55:21,920 --> 00:55:24,040
So you want to talk game?
Who's going home tonight?

1064
00:55:25,000 --> 00:55:28,160
Where? What?
Who are we taking out tonight?

1065
00:55:28,160 --> 00:55:29,800
Yeah, you tell me.
You have the numbers.

1066
00:55:29,800 --> 00:55:30,840
You tell me.

1067
00:55:32,680 --> 00:55:35,520
What do you think?
You guys have four right here.

1068
00:55:35,520 --> 00:55:38,120
You're looking at me,
trying to ask me to tell you.

1069
00:55:39,480 --> 00:55:40,960
Ha-ha, we just lost one now.

1070
00:55:40,960 --> 00:55:42,680
(LAUGHTER)

1071
00:55:42,680 --> 00:55:43,720
Are you OK?

1072
00:55:43,720 --> 00:55:45,600
Nice try, buddy.

1073
00:55:45,600 --> 00:55:47,080
OK, so what do you say?

1074
00:55:47,080 --> 00:55:48,680
What do you think we do?
What do you say?

1075
00:55:55,640 --> 00:55:57,720
I'm waiting
to hear your suggestion.

1076
00:55:57,720 --> 00:55:59,920
How does Cirie sound?

1077
00:55:59,920 --> 00:56:02,480
What?
How does Cirie sound?

1078
00:56:03,640 --> 00:56:05,160
Cirie?
Yeah.

1079
00:56:05,160 --> 00:56:08,000
I mean, I love Cirie, but...

1080
00:56:08,000 --> 00:56:09,880
I know we do as well.

1081
00:56:09,880 --> 00:56:12,080
You guys are trying
to get a forum.

1082
00:56:12,080 --> 00:56:14,040
Trying to keep the tribe strong,
that's all.

1083
00:56:21,840 --> 00:56:23,880
We're not being unfair
or unreasonable.

1084
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:27,880
And I think that's a very simplistic
way of looking at this,

1085
00:56:27,880 --> 00:56:29,360
the tribe dynamics.

1086
00:56:29,360 --> 00:56:33,800
This is a game of lots of different
people and personalities.

1087
00:56:33,800 --> 00:56:37,160
So, there's
a lot of things to consider.

1088
00:56:37,160 --> 00:56:38,680
So, I'll ask again. Then who?

1089
00:56:39,800 --> 00:56:41,920
Then who?
Then I need to think about it.

1090
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:44,400
I think everyone needs to have
conversations with each other.

1091
00:56:44,400 --> 00:56:48,280
We have an afternoon to talk about
it and figure it out.

1092
00:56:48,280 --> 00:56:52,480
I try to give Parvati a beautiful
ticket out of this nonsense,

1093
00:56:52,480 --> 00:56:55,680
and she just rejected it
to my face.

1094
00:56:55,680 --> 00:56:57,560
So she has to go home.

1095
00:57:20,880 --> 00:57:24,480
The set-up is perfect.
We've got four players.

1096
00:57:27,600 --> 00:57:31,200
Let me go to Tony and Cirie
and bring them in on it.

1097
00:57:31,200 --> 00:57:34,920
If I get this right, that means
I am able to unify this tribe.

1098
00:57:34,920 --> 00:57:36,720
And that's what I need.

1099
00:57:36,720 --> 00:57:38,320
I need soldiers
to fight the oncoming battle.

1100
00:57:38,320 --> 00:57:40,720
What are your thoughts? Uh, Rob?

1101
00:57:40,720 --> 00:57:43,000
I came to find out
from you guys.

1102
00:57:43,000 --> 00:57:44,000
Where are your heads at?

1103
00:57:44,000 --> 00:57:45,360
I haven't scrambled with nobody.

1104
00:57:45,360 --> 00:57:47,600
I'm asking Cirie,
is anybody talking game to her?

1105
00:57:47,600 --> 00:57:49,880
Nobody's talking game to her
either.

1106
00:57:49,880 --> 00:57:51,760
Has anybody talked game to you?
Yeah.

1107
00:57:51,760 --> 00:57:54,000
People are trying to figure out
what to do.

1108
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:56,320
OK. What are people
saying to you?

1109
00:57:56,320 --> 00:57:58,720
Are they saying, let's break
up the threat, get rid of Tony?

1110
00:57:58,720 --> 00:58:00,480
Or are they saying
stuff like that?

1111
00:58:00,480 --> 00:58:01,480
No.
OK.

1112
00:58:01,480 --> 00:58:03,040
OK. That's... I can tell you
straightaway.

1113
00:58:03,040 --> 00:58:06,040
OK.
No-one has said Tony.

1114
00:58:09,200 --> 00:58:10,480
Yeah, yeah.

1115
00:58:10,480 --> 00:58:12,680
It's being swung around a bit.

1116
00:58:12,680 --> 00:58:16,000
Um, I think you should... You should
go and chat to people.

1117
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:19,760
People's biggest fear
is too many Americans.

1118
00:58:32,520 --> 00:58:34,720
Listen, if the group...

1119
00:58:34,720 --> 00:58:36,640
You're telling me my name
is on the chopping block?

1120
00:58:36,640 --> 00:58:37,640
Yes.

1121
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:46,680
I'm going with the numbers, man.
Exactly.

1122
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:51,120
Of course, Rob believes that I'm
doing exactly as I'm told.

1123
00:58:51,120 --> 00:58:53,000
Why wouldn't I listen to the king?

1124
00:58:56,720 --> 00:59:02,240
But listen, me and Parv rode before,
and this is not our first rodeo.

1125
00:59:13,920 --> 00:59:16,560
I've talked to you earlier.
That doesn't count.

1126
00:59:16,560 --> 00:59:17,960
Why doesn't it count?

1127
00:59:17,960 --> 00:59:19,520
That wasn't a real talk.

1128
00:59:21,600 --> 00:59:23,880
Then let's go talk.
Yeah.

1129
00:59:23,880 --> 00:59:25,360
OK.

1130
00:59:25,360 --> 00:59:29,160
I have been investing time
and energy into Rob.

1131
00:59:29,160 --> 00:59:31,680
I wanted this to work
between us.

1132
00:59:33,440 --> 00:59:35,280
Is this your game?
What?

1133
00:59:35,280 --> 00:59:39,080
You just try to bulldoze people into
doing what you want them to do.

1134
00:59:47,120 --> 00:59:49,880
I literally brought you in
with the four people

1135
00:59:49,880 --> 00:59:51,120
and I said, "Hey, join us."

1136
00:59:51,120 --> 00:59:54,560
I literally gave you, like,
everything you ever wanted

1137
00:59:54,560 --> 00:59:56,440
because I trusted you so much.

1138
00:59:56,440 --> 00:59:59,560
It's been so good since day one.
We've been great.

1139
00:59:59,560 --> 01:00:02,720
But now I feel like I'm completely
missing the mark with you,

1140
01:00:02,720 --> 01:00:05,040
because I feel like

1141
01:00:05,040 --> 01:00:09,360
you maybe have a big group of people
that you want to work with.

1142
01:00:09,360 --> 01:00:12,320
I don't see us as a group.
I see us as a you and me.

1143
01:00:12,320 --> 01:00:13,720
What name do you have in mind?

1144
01:00:13,720 --> 01:00:16,880
I can't say a name because
you're working with all of them.

1145
01:00:21,360 --> 01:00:23,320
She's one of the people
that I trust here.

1146
01:00:23,320 --> 01:00:25,440
I don't trust a lot of people
here. I trust her.

1147
01:00:25,440 --> 01:00:27,080
Who do you want to vote for?

1148
01:00:27,080 --> 01:00:28,760
I don't know,
vote for somebody else.

1149
01:00:30,520 --> 01:00:33,520
Whoever. Who do you want me
to vote for besides her?

1150
01:00:35,960 --> 01:00:39,720
It was a long-term plan to try
to keep the tribe strong thing.

1151
01:00:39,720 --> 01:00:42,800
Tell me.
Doesn't matter now anyway.

1152
01:00:42,800 --> 01:00:45,080
It doesn't matter now
because you're voting for me.

1153
01:00:45,080 --> 01:00:46,080
No, I didn't say that.

1154
01:00:50,920 --> 01:00:55,440
I mean, I'm, like,
I'm so offended.

1155
01:00:55,440 --> 01:00:58,880
I know that he's trying
to blindside me tonight.

1156
01:00:58,880 --> 01:01:01,880
Sir, you do not know
who you're messing with.

1157
01:01:01,880 --> 01:01:06,040
You don't, like, you don't blindside
the queen. You don't.

1158
01:01:13,400 --> 01:01:16,520
Where is everybody?
I have no idea. I'm just...

1159
01:01:17,840 --> 01:01:21,480
People are scrambling.
It's... It's unbelievable.

1160
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:31,160
You're relaxed, you're calm.
Relaxed.

1161
01:01:35,080 --> 01:01:37,880
Rob thinks he's running this tribe.

1162
01:01:37,880 --> 01:01:40,240
So don't you usually
cut the head of the snake off?

1163
01:01:40,240 --> 01:01:42,600
Because we can't
have Rob telling Tommi,

1164
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:46,120
Lisa, Kass, potentially Tony
what to do.

1165
01:01:46,120 --> 01:01:47,320
So Rob has to go.

1166
01:01:54,000 --> 01:01:56,480
So Rob suggested I talk to everybody

1167
01:01:56,480 --> 01:01:59,240
since my name
is being floated around.

1168
01:01:59,240 --> 01:02:00,560
By him.
Exactly.

1169
01:02:00,560 --> 01:02:03,240
I know,
but he's trying to make me think

1170
01:02:03,240 --> 01:02:05,640
that all of you are saying my name.

1171
01:02:08,440 --> 01:02:09,440
Huh?

1172
01:02:10,680 --> 01:02:13,520
Rob's plan is to vote out Parvati,

1173
01:02:13,520 --> 01:02:19,440
and he just wants me, Kass and
Tommi to just go along with it

1174
01:02:19,440 --> 01:02:22,240
because it's best
for us to just stay as a group.

1175
01:02:22,240 --> 01:02:24,880
But I don't
know how anyone thinks it's OK

1176
01:02:24,880 --> 01:02:28,120
to just dictate to people, like,
I don't know if you know this,

1177
01:02:28,120 --> 01:02:30,040
but I already won Survivor,

1178
01:02:30,040 --> 01:02:32,520
so I think I might know
what to do a little bit.

1179
01:02:32,520 --> 01:02:35,040
I'm so glad
Rob's working it out for us.

1180
01:02:35,040 --> 01:02:36,640
I wouldn't know what to do
if he wasn't.

1181
01:02:36,640 --> 01:02:40,000
My question though,
is who would vote Rob?

1182
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:41,680
I would definitely vote Rob.

1183
01:02:41,680 --> 01:02:43,320
I know you would definitely
vote Rob.

1184
01:02:43,320 --> 01:02:44,600
Rob yesterday.

1185
01:02:45,560 --> 01:02:48,480
He's so good at everything.
Like starting a fire,

1186
01:02:48,480 --> 01:02:52,480
using a slingshot,
keeping track of a machete.

1187
01:02:52,480 --> 01:02:53,920
Do you see it?

1188
01:02:57,520 --> 01:02:59,760
(LAUGHTER)

1189
01:02:59,760 --> 01:03:02,200
Wait, I'm sorry I had to laugh,
like, you...

1190
01:03:02,200 --> 01:03:03,720
He sold a lot of tickets

1191
01:03:03,720 --> 01:03:06,880
that he has not delivered
on any of them yet.

1192
01:03:08,200 --> 01:03:11,760
For a first vote, Rob.
Very sensible.

1193
01:03:11,760 --> 01:03:16,760
But, um,
this is probably so stupid,

1194
01:03:16,760 --> 01:03:19,360
but I want to play with Cirie.

1195
01:03:19,360 --> 01:03:21,680
I want to play with Cirie.

1196
01:03:21,680 --> 01:03:25,640
Just us together. I just want that
to happen so bad.

1197
01:03:26,680 --> 01:03:30,680
If Parvati goes home tonight, it is
good for my relationship with Cirie.

1198
01:03:43,000 --> 01:03:45,280
Yeah.
After that...

1199
01:03:45,280 --> 01:03:46,360
Ladies.

1200
01:03:48,600 --> 01:03:50,400
I'm starting to get so stressed.

1201
01:03:50,400 --> 01:03:53,000
Every time I walk up to the
shelter, everyone stops talking.

1202
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:54,560
I feel like I'm getting
blindsided.

1203
01:03:56,560 --> 01:03:58,880
Is it me?
I don't know.

1204
01:03:58,880 --> 01:03:59,920
Is it me?

1205
01:04:01,200 --> 01:04:02,640
Oh, my God. It's me.

1206
01:04:09,720 --> 01:04:11,360
Rob threw my name.
But...

1207
01:04:11,360 --> 01:04:12,920
Well, that's what I heard.

1208
01:04:21,400 --> 01:04:23,240
He thinks he's in charge.

1209
01:04:24,520 --> 01:04:26,280
And it's a little bit hard to...

1210
01:04:29,520 --> 01:04:31,320
What do we want to do?

1211
01:04:35,320 --> 01:04:39,120
I'll go with you girls, like, 100%.

1212
01:04:52,880 --> 01:04:55,960
OK. The rest of the girls
I think are OK with that.

1213
01:04:55,960 --> 01:04:58,840
We have to.
I'm doing it.

1214
01:05:02,280 --> 01:05:03,800
No! Stop! Stop, stop!

1215
01:05:03,800 --> 01:05:07,120
It's Rob. Rob. It's Rob!
It's Rob. Rob!

1216
01:05:10,360 --> 01:05:12,480
Say no more. I'm OK.
Alright.

1217
01:05:30,400 --> 01:05:33,600
My goodness.
I need to take a swim.

1218
01:05:41,920 --> 01:05:45,160
LISA: At the moment, I'm in
a pretty powerful position.

1219
01:05:45,160 --> 01:05:47,520
This is like, full-on Survivor.

1220
01:05:47,520 --> 01:05:48,600
So...
Yes.

1221
01:05:48,600 --> 01:05:50,240
I don't want to...

1222
01:05:53,800 --> 01:05:57,240
Yeah. I don't want to sound like
Rob, but Parvati or Rob.

1223
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:08,360
Yeah.
They are both equal threat.

1224
01:06:08,360 --> 01:06:09,720
What do you think?

1225
01:06:14,640 --> 01:06:15,960
I'm just trying to think.

1226
01:06:42,280 --> 01:06:45,760
Pulling off this blindside means
the Black Widow is back.

1227
01:06:47,080 --> 01:06:52,680
I'm aligned with Tony and Cirie,
with Lisa, and with Kass.

1228
01:06:52,680 --> 01:06:55,600
So I think
we're going to vote Rob.

1229
01:06:55,600 --> 01:06:56,920
If I'm not being played,

1230
01:06:56,920 --> 01:06:59,640
which I could totally
be being played right now,

1231
01:06:59,640 --> 01:07:01,440
I'm aware of that.
This is Survivor.

1232
01:07:02,640 --> 01:07:06,880
So it's completely possible
that I'm aligned with nobody.

1233
01:07:39,120 --> 01:07:41,520
Alright, you know the drill.
Go ahead.

1234
01:07:41,520 --> 01:07:44,280
Grab a torch, come forward,
dip it in and get fire.

1235
01:07:47,240 --> 01:07:49,800
It's part of
the ritual of Tribal Council.

1236
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:53,680
Because in this game,
fire represents your life.

1237
01:07:53,680 --> 01:07:56,760
Once it's gone, so are you.

1238
01:08:04,560 --> 01:08:06,680
Alright.

1239
01:08:06,680 --> 01:08:09,400
Parvati,
you've played more Survivor

1240
01:08:09,400 --> 01:08:11,880
than almost anyone else
in the world.

1241
01:08:11,880 --> 01:08:15,640
How does this game differ from
the other ones you've played?

1242
01:08:16,760 --> 01:08:18,640
Um, there's a lot
of differences here.

1243
01:08:18,640 --> 01:08:19,920
I think we're all kind of
adjusting

1244
01:08:19,920 --> 01:08:23,280
to how do we relate to each
other from different countries?

1245
01:08:23,280 --> 01:08:26,480
I've never had that experience
on Survivor before

1246
01:08:26,480 --> 01:08:29,040
and this game is pretty fast.

1247
01:08:29,040 --> 01:08:31,040
We're on day two.

1248
01:08:31,040 --> 01:08:32,800
We're looking at, like,

1249
01:08:32,800 --> 01:08:36,280
there's people crossing lines
at challenges,

1250
01:08:36,280 --> 01:08:38,040
trying to talk to the other side.

1251
01:08:40,360 --> 01:08:41,400
Rob, is that true?

1252
01:08:41,400 --> 01:08:44,440
Are people crossing lines
already with the other tribe?

1253
01:08:45,720 --> 01:08:48,400
Yes. Conversations are happening.

1254
01:08:48,400 --> 01:08:50,960
In Survivor,
you always have to listen,

1255
01:08:50,960 --> 01:08:52,240
especially to your enemy.

1256
01:08:52,240 --> 01:08:54,560
It's the Australians
versus the World.

1257
01:08:54,560 --> 01:08:58,000
If we hit merge and there's more
Australians than us,

1258
01:08:58,000 --> 01:08:59,560
we are all doomed.

1259
01:09:01,560 --> 01:09:02,680
Cirie.

1260
01:09:02,680 --> 01:09:06,120
How would you characterise
the pace of this game so far?

1261
01:09:07,800 --> 01:09:08,920
Um...

1262
01:09:10,880 --> 01:09:13,000
I would say top speed.

1263
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:15,920
The game started
the second we hit the mats.

1264
01:09:15,920 --> 01:09:19,120
The game started the second you saw
people having conversations

1265
01:09:19,120 --> 01:09:21,440
and they weren't having those
conversations with you.

1266
01:09:21,440 --> 01:09:24,960
And typically, if conversations are
being had and you're not included,

1267
01:09:24,960 --> 01:09:26,240
you're probably in trouble.

1268
01:09:26,240 --> 01:09:28,360
Has that been the case for you?

1269
01:09:28,360 --> 01:09:30,240
Um...

1270
01:09:33,200 --> 01:09:37,280
Well, I think maybe it shifted
a little bit.

1271
01:09:37,280 --> 01:09:39,320
Initially, there wasn't
a lot of conversations,

1272
01:09:39,320 --> 01:09:44,080
but I feel a little bit better now
with conversations that I've had.

1273
01:09:47,960 --> 01:09:50,760
So, Tony, an obvious division
in this tribe

1274
01:09:50,760 --> 01:09:53,720
is three US players
against four players

1275
01:09:53,720 --> 01:09:55,280
who are not from the US.

1276
01:09:55,280 --> 01:09:58,360
Do you think that's going
to factor into tonight?

1277
01:09:58,360 --> 01:10:01,720
I hope not, Jonathan. I mean,
we're all here as tribe mates.

1278
01:10:01,720 --> 01:10:05,240
We're not from South Africa,
we're not from America.

1279
01:10:05,240 --> 01:10:08,800
We're just tribe mates that got
challenged by the Aussies.

1280
01:10:08,800 --> 01:10:10,920
And that's all that's on my mind.

1281
01:10:13,240 --> 01:10:16,440
But, Rob,
surely that's a valid strategy

1282
01:10:16,440 --> 01:10:20,480
for the four non-Americans
to stick together.

1283
01:10:22,120 --> 01:10:23,200
Possibly.

1284
01:10:23,200 --> 01:10:27,640
But the problem there is that you
then alienate people going forward.

1285
01:10:27,640 --> 01:10:29,920
So I believe it's not the time

1286
01:10:29,920 --> 01:10:33,440
to blindside anyone in this tribe
right now.

1287
01:10:33,440 --> 01:10:34,680
And I'm hoping and praying

1288
01:10:34,680 --> 01:10:38,320
that we can prove something that's
been very seldom done on Survivor,

1289
01:10:38,320 --> 01:10:41,120
where we can do a vote
that is 100% unified.

1290
01:10:43,600 --> 01:10:49,480
Yeah, Kass, it can't be 100% unified
because someone's going home tonight.

1291
01:10:49,480 --> 01:10:53,680
Yeah. Of course.
Um, but it can be close.

1292
01:10:55,480 --> 01:10:59,320
Parvati, are you concerned
that these non-Americans

1293
01:10:59,320 --> 01:11:02,360
are conspiring to take out
one of the Americans?

1294
01:11:02,360 --> 01:11:04,800
Yes. Very much.

1295
01:11:04,800 --> 01:11:08,640
That's been shared with me.

1296
01:11:08,640 --> 01:11:11,840
It's a clear way to divide the tribe
if we have to go to a vote.

1297
01:11:11,840 --> 01:11:13,360
Majority rules.

1298
01:11:13,360 --> 01:11:17,160
And if you're in the majority,
you have the power.

1299
01:11:21,360 --> 01:11:25,720
Cirie, usually at this stage
of any game of Survivor,

1300
01:11:25,720 --> 01:11:28,840
the conversation
turns to tribe strength.

1301
01:11:28,840 --> 01:11:31,440
Did that happen this afternoon?

1302
01:11:31,440 --> 01:11:33,040
Um, yeah, that was mentioned.

1303
01:11:33,040 --> 01:11:36,760
It was mentioned, but I kind
of think tribe strength

1304
01:11:36,760 --> 01:11:41,040
presents itself in many shapes
and colours, right?

1305
01:11:41,040 --> 01:11:45,120
So, if you're saying
tribe physical strength,

1306
01:11:45,120 --> 01:11:47,760
um, that's one aspect
of the game.

1307
01:11:47,760 --> 01:11:50,000
But the game is not
just physicality.

1308
01:11:51,520 --> 01:11:53,440
I definitely, I do agree, um,
with that,

1309
01:11:53,440 --> 01:11:56,560
physical strength is not the only
most important thing in this game.

1310
01:11:56,560 --> 01:11:59,560
And it's also looking at who you can
work with going forward

1311
01:11:59,560 --> 01:12:03,160
when we do start intertwining
with the other tribe,

1312
01:12:03,160 --> 01:12:04,560
because if one person cracks,

1313
01:12:04,560 --> 01:12:07,760
then they get through
and they annihilate us all.

1314
01:12:07,760 --> 01:12:10,560
So that kind of strength,
that mental fortitude,

1315
01:12:10,560 --> 01:12:14,600
that strength
to actually hold our line,

1316
01:12:14,600 --> 01:12:16,480
that is actually truly
the most important thing.

1317
01:12:16,480 --> 01:12:18,800
And that is basically
boiled down to loyalty.

1318
01:12:20,720 --> 01:12:24,400
Tonight is the first of many tests,
and each time we pass the test,

1319
01:12:24,400 --> 01:12:26,680
the loyalty and trust
get stronger.

1320
01:12:26,680 --> 01:12:29,120
So that means you want to keep
coming back to Tribal Council

1321
01:12:29,120 --> 01:12:30,120
to keep making tests?

1322
01:12:30,120 --> 01:12:32,480
No, no. Hopefully this is the last
time we come back like this.

1323
01:12:32,480 --> 01:12:33,880
Next time we come back,

1324
01:12:33,880 --> 01:12:37,720
there'll be Aussies amongst us
that we can take out.

1325
01:12:37,720 --> 01:12:38,720
Together.

1326
01:12:38,720 --> 01:12:40,120
Then how do you test that?

1327
01:12:44,680 --> 01:12:46,360
Well, I know that.

1328
01:12:46,360 --> 01:12:48,800
Because there's something
you didn't tell the tribe.

1329
01:12:51,200 --> 01:12:52,520
What?

1330
01:12:54,960 --> 01:12:56,440
I know about you and David.

1331
01:13:14,240 --> 01:13:15,600
I know about you and David.

1332
01:13:18,680 --> 01:13:20,720
She was going to turn on us first.

1333
01:13:22,840 --> 01:13:26,280
The second she got to David,
she was going to turn on us.

1334
01:13:26,280 --> 01:13:29,240
She leaked it yesterday.
That is not what happened.

1335
01:13:29,240 --> 01:13:31,640
I told Rob that David and I

1336
01:13:31,640 --> 01:13:34,800
played a game called Deal
or No Deal Island together.

1337
01:13:34,800 --> 01:13:38,640
And David loves Rob.

1338
01:13:38,640 --> 01:13:42,160
She made it clear that they played
well together in that game

1339
01:13:42,160 --> 01:13:44,080
and they went very far together.

1340
01:13:44,080 --> 01:13:46,680
That tells me that they have
a good relationship,

1341
01:13:46,680 --> 01:13:51,000
and I'm very petrified of
the day they get together again.

1342
01:13:54,320 --> 01:13:56,880
This is very interesting.

1343
01:13:56,880 --> 01:14:00,280
This is very interesting coming
from you at this moment

1344
01:14:00,280 --> 01:14:02,880
after we've seen you
communicating with David

1345
01:14:02,880 --> 01:14:04,880
multiple times in the challenges.

1346
01:14:04,880 --> 01:14:06,000
He comes to me.

1347
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:10,440
And it's been very clear that
you want to work with David.

1348
01:14:10,440 --> 01:14:14,680
I know David from that game
that I played.

1349
01:14:14,680 --> 01:14:17,560
We played together
until he threw me under the bus.

1350
01:14:20,320 --> 01:14:23,200
Now we know what happened.
That's the deal.

1351
01:14:23,200 --> 01:14:25,760
I'm not watching no more.
Deal or No Deal Island.

1352
01:14:30,200 --> 01:14:34,040
Lisa, I saw you down the end
with a big smile.

1353
01:14:34,040 --> 01:14:36,760
What's going through your head?

1354
01:14:36,760 --> 01:14:39,360
First of all, spoilers
for Deal or No Deal Island.

1355
01:14:39,360 --> 01:14:41,600
Like, thanks, guys.

1356
01:14:41,600 --> 01:14:43,840
Yeah, I hadn't heard anything
about that.

1357
01:14:43,840 --> 01:14:46,720
And I guess it just shows, like,
what sort of game this is, like,

1358
01:14:46,720 --> 01:14:51,160
it's so fast that, like, apparently
a whole storyline situation

1359
01:14:51,160 --> 01:14:56,000
can be happening that crosses over
the reality TV multiverse.

1360
01:14:56,000 --> 01:14:59,160
And I'm just in the dark about it.
It's a Survivor first.

1361
01:14:59,160 --> 01:15:00,600
Bucket list. Tick.

1362
01:15:03,240 --> 01:15:05,720
So, Cirie,
what's your position on this?

1363
01:15:05,720 --> 01:15:11,040
Are you concerned that there's new
information coming out at Tribal?

1364
01:15:11,040 --> 01:15:15,280
Um, I'd be foolish not to say
it raises an eyebrow.

1365
01:15:15,280 --> 01:15:17,120
Um...

1366
01:15:17,120 --> 01:15:22,720
..but whether she played
Deal or No Deal with David or not,

1367
01:15:22,720 --> 01:15:26,200
um, doesn't affect the relationships
that I'm building here.

1368
01:15:28,440 --> 01:15:31,080
So, Parvati, what's tonight's vote
about for you?

1369
01:15:32,320 --> 01:15:34,000
Well, for me,
I'm voting out the person

1370
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:35,760
who's trying to blindside
or not even.

1371
01:15:35,760 --> 01:15:37,440
It's not a blindside anymore.

1372
01:15:37,440 --> 01:15:39,920
It's very clear
that he wants to vote me out.

1373
01:15:39,920 --> 01:15:42,720
So, I just think that what Rob
has done

1374
01:15:42,720 --> 01:15:45,200
to try to throw a huge target on me

1375
01:15:45,200 --> 01:15:48,760
is helping him
try to get the target off of him.

1376
01:15:54,400 --> 01:15:56,400
I don't really get down with someone

1377
01:15:56,400 --> 01:15:59,040
who wants to have control over
everybody else.

1378
01:15:59,040 --> 01:16:02,400
So I think I've made it clear
where my vote is going.

1379
01:16:07,360 --> 01:16:10,200
Alright, well,

1380
01:16:10,200 --> 01:16:12,280
I think it might be time to vote.

1381
01:16:12,280 --> 01:16:14,160
Yeah. Because I've got a question.

1382
01:16:39,920 --> 01:16:43,760
Alright. It is time to vote.
Cirie, you're up.

1383
01:16:43,760 --> 01:16:45,560
Lucky me.

1384
01:16:51,920 --> 01:16:53,360
Why did I have to go first?

1385
01:16:56,480 --> 01:16:58,400
Well, here goes nothing.

1386
01:17:23,800 --> 01:17:28,320
This is just a backup
in case an idol gets played.

1387
01:17:45,960 --> 01:17:48,760
You tried
to blindside me on my birthday.

1388
01:17:48,760 --> 01:17:51,360
I'm not mad.
I'm just disappointed.

1389
01:17:59,880 --> 01:18:01,080
I'll go count the votes.

1390
01:18:18,000 --> 01:18:19,920
If anyone has an idol
and you want to play it,

1391
01:18:19,920 --> 01:18:21,720
now would be the time to do so.

1392
01:18:35,440 --> 01:18:37,720
Alright, I'll read the votes.

1393
01:18:42,320 --> 01:18:45,040
First vote. Cirie.

1394
01:18:51,160 --> 01:18:52,560
Rob.

1395
01:18:53,800 --> 01:18:55,800
That's one vote Cirie. One vote Rob.

1396
01:19:01,520 --> 01:19:02,720
Rob.

1397
01:19:05,720 --> 01:19:08,160
That's two votes Rob.
One vote Cirie.

1398
01:19:12,960 --> 01:19:14,160
Rob.

1399
01:19:16,680 --> 01:19:19,080
Three votes Rob.
One vote Cirie.

1400
01:19:25,480 --> 01:19:28,400
First person voted out
of Australia versus the World.

1401
01:19:30,080 --> 01:19:31,160
Rob.

1402
01:19:36,880 --> 01:19:40,880
That's four votes. That's enough.
You need to bring me your torch.

1403
01:19:40,880 --> 01:19:42,680
Good job.

1404
01:19:49,840 --> 01:19:51,800
Rob, the tribe has spoken.

1405
01:19:55,160 --> 01:19:56,800
That's it. Time for you to go.

1406
01:19:58,240 --> 01:19:59,760
Cheers, mate. Good luck, guys.

1407
01:19:59,760 --> 01:20:00,760
Bye, Rob.
Bye.

1408
01:20:06,440 --> 01:20:09,720
Well, this tribe might want
to be the United Nations,

1409
01:20:09,720 --> 01:20:15,120
but one thing is clear,
World peace is a long way off.

1410
01:20:15,120 --> 01:20:17,800
Before you go,
I've got something for you.

1411
01:20:17,800 --> 01:20:19,440
You might need this.

1412
01:20:20,440 --> 01:20:23,400
There you go, Lisa.
Alright. Grab your torches.

1413
01:20:23,400 --> 01:20:24,800
Head back to camp. Good night.

1414
01:20:38,280 --> 01:20:41,040
Australia's most notorious players...

1415
01:20:41,040 --> 01:20:44,520
GEORGE: Golden God
up against the best-ever winner.

1416
01:20:44,520 --> 01:20:46,640
..take on global megastars...

1417
01:20:46,640 --> 01:20:48,720
If you come for me
and I didn't send for you,

1418
01:20:48,720 --> 01:20:50,320
you're going
to get your torch snuffed.

1419
01:20:50,320 --> 01:20:51,960
..in a supercharged season...

1420
01:20:51,960 --> 01:20:54,960
This is like playing
in a grand final every single day.

1421
01:20:54,960 --> 01:20:58,440
..where the highest honour
is up for grabs.

1422
01:20:58,440 --> 01:21:00,960
I'm here for the glory.
I want the world title.

1423
01:21:00,960 --> 01:21:02,040
But only one...

1424
01:21:02,040 --> 01:21:05,080
I'm coming in here guns blazing,
ready to win.

1425
01:21:05,080 --> 01:21:06,440
..can be the world's first...

1426
01:21:06,440 --> 01:21:10,400
Everybody will bend their knee
to their king.

1427
01:21:10,400 --> 01:21:11,840
..international...

1428
01:21:11,840 --> 01:21:13,480
Come on, let's go, Aussie.

1429
01:21:13,480 --> 01:21:15,200
..sole survivor.

1430
01:21:15,200 --> 01:21:17,040
Let's get this party started.

1431
01:21:20,520 --> 01:21:22,520
World tribe
decided to blindside me.

1432
01:21:22,520 --> 01:21:24,080
I can kind of understand why.

1433
01:21:24,080 --> 01:21:26,120
Um, massive threat in the game.

1434
01:21:26,120 --> 01:21:30,360
I was the only thing standing
between them and the Australians.

1435
01:21:30,360 --> 01:21:32,840
And now they
will be sliced apart.

1436
01:21:32,840 --> 01:21:37,320
Rob. I'm so sorry, man, but you
interfered with the mission

1437
01:21:37,320 --> 01:21:39,600
the Americans were sent here
to accomplish.

1438
01:21:40,880 --> 01:21:42,680
I truly thought
they had brains in them

1439
01:21:42,680 --> 01:21:44,960
to realise that the only way to
beat the Australians

1440
01:21:44,960 --> 01:21:46,240
is to work together as a team.

1441
01:21:48,120 --> 01:21:51,440
I can 100% guarantee an Aussie
will win sole survivor now.

1442
01:21:51,440 --> 01:21:54,200
Without a shadow of doubt.

1443
01:21:54,200 --> 01:21:56,280
Captions by Red Bee Media
